 "result_text": "I fixed it in `nose2/session.py`. `nose2 -c tox.ini` should now load your `[unittest]` plugins, so `--junit-xml` is recognised again. I haven't run it or the tests.\n\nIn 0.15.0, `loadConfigFiles` only read files ending in `.cfg` and `pyproject.toml`. A `tox.ini` was silently skipped, so your `plugins =` list was never loaded and the junitxml plugin never registered its option.\n\nAny file ending in `.toml` is now parsed as TOML. Every other file is parsed as ini, so `tox.ini` and other `.ini` files work, as does anything else passed with `-c`. I widened the TOML check from `pyproject.toml` to any `.toml` file, so a differently named TOML file passed with `-c` is now parsed as TOML instead of being skipped.",
